Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "Track"."TrackId": primary key to join with "InvoiceLine"."TrackId".  
• "Track"."Milliseconds": raw duration of every track – will be converted to minutes and used for the short / medium / long classification.  
• "Track"."Name": handy for quick sanity checks while exploring data.  
• "InvoiceLine"."TrackId": foreign‑key link to the corresponding track.  
• "InvoiceLine"."Quantity": number of units sold for that line.  
• "InvoiceLine"."UnitPrice": price per unit – revenue for the line equals UnitPrice × Quantity.  
(Everything else in the schema is not needed for this particular task.)

Typical conditions we may use during exploration  
• Durations:  
  – short  : "Track"."Milliseconds" < 180000 (≈3:00)  
  – medium : "Track"."Milliseconds" BETWEEN 180000 AND 300000 (≈3:00–5:00)  
  – long   : "Track"."Milliseconds" > 300000 (≥5:00)  
• Revenue calculation: ("InvoiceLine"."UnitPrice" * "InvoiceLine"."Quantity").  
• Joins: "Track"."TrackId" = "InvoiceLine"."TrackId".

Below are ten example SQLite queries—starting simple and getting progressively closer to the final goal.  
Every query is preceded by a brief comment and capped with LIMIT 20 so you can inspect a small slice of the data first.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct raw millisecond values just to see what they look like
SELECT DISTINCT "Milliseconds"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Convert milliseconds to minutes (rounded to 2 decimals) for the first 20 tracks
SELECT "TrackId",
       ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2) AS "Minutes"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Sample track names with their durations in minutes
SELECT "Name",
       ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2) AS "Minutes"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Check how many tracks fall into each ad‑hoc length bucket
SELECT CASE
         WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'short'
         WHEN "Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'medium'
         ELSE 'long'
       END AS "length_category",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_tracks"
FROM "Track"
GROUP BY "length_category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Look at 20 short tracks (<3 minutes) to verify classification
SELECT "TrackId", "Name",
       ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2) AS "Minutes"
FROM "Track"
WHERE "Milliseconds" < 180000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Join "Track" with "InvoiceLine" to see revenue per track instance
SELECT il."InvoiceLineId",
       il."TrackId",
       (il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "line_revenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine" AS il
JOIN "Track" AS t ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate total revenue for each individual track
SELECT il."TrackId",
       SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "total_revenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine" AS il
GROUP BY il."TrackId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Classify tracks and calculate revenue per classification bucket
SELECT CASE
         WHEN t."Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'short'
         WHEN t."Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'medium'
         ELSE 'long'
       END AS "length_category",
       SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "bucket_revenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine" AS il
JOIN "Track"       AS t ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
GROUP BY "length_category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Determine minimum and maximum minutes within each length bucket
SELECT CASE
         WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'short'
         WHEN "Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'medium'
         ELSE 'long'
       END AS "length_category",
       MIN(ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2)) AS "min_minutes",
       MAX(ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2)) AS "max_minutes"
FROM "Track"
GROUP BY "length_category"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Bring it all together: bucket, min/max minutes, and total revenue
SELECT bucket."length_category",
       bucket."min_minutes",
       bucket."max_minutes",
       rev."bucket_revenue"
FROM (
      -- sub‑query for min / max
      SELECT CASE
               WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'short'
               WHEN "Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'medium'
               ELSE 'long'
             END AS "length_category",
             MIN(ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2)) AS "min_minutes",
             MAX(ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2)) AS "max_minutes"
      FROM "Track"
      GROUP BY "length_category"
     ) AS bucket
JOIN (
      -- sub‑query for revenue
      SELECT CASE
               WHEN t."Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'short'
               WHEN t."Milliseconds" <= 300000 THEN 'medium'
               ELSE 'long'
             END AS "length_category",
             SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "bucket_revenue"
      FROM "InvoiceLine" AS il
      JOIN "Track"       AS t ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
      GROUP BY "length_category"
     ) AS rev
ON bucket."length_category" = rev."length_category"
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries let you inspect durations, validate the short/medium/long thresholds, and confirm the revenue figures before producing the final grouped report.
